6],"k":"quotation","m":"editionCitation","c":"high","cited":"[\"Εν ἐμοί means `in my mind, 0' `in my consciousness. 0' 2 Cor iv: 6,\" in opposition to Lightfoot who says, \"`In me 0' means, as the context shows, not a revelation made inwardly to himself, but through him to others.\"-G. A.]"},{"id":"2e6335057297","b":"LUK","v":"npnf.chrysostomus.comm_gal","w":"chrysostomus.comm_gal","a":"johannes_chrysostomus","s":2,"p":[55,55],"r":[10,22],"k":"quotation","m":"editionCitation","c":"high","cited":"Luke x: 22"},{"id":"4a64f8af0376","b":"JHN","v":"npnf.chrysostomus.comm_gal","w":"chrysostomus.comm_gal","a":"johannes_chrysostomus","s":2,"p":[55,55],"r":[17,1],"k":"quotation","m":"editionCitation","c":"high","cited":"John xvii: 1"},{"id":"a3907ef115d6","b":"JHN","v":"npnf.chrysostomus.comm_gal","w":"chrysostomus.comm_gal","a":"johannes_chrysostomus","s":2,"p":[55,55],"r":[17,4],"k":"quotation","m":"editionCitation","c":"high","cited":"John xvii: 4"},{"id":"6b6bea904a0a","b":"MAT","v":"npnf.chrysostomus.comm_gal","w":"chrysostomus.comm_gal","a":"johannes_chrysostomus","s":2,"p":[58,58],"r":[16,17],"k":"quotation","m":"editionCitation","c":"high","cited":"[\"Flesh and blood,\" is twice used elsewhere (Mat. 16:17 and Eph. 6:12,) to denote \"weak human nature,\" \"feeble man.\"-G. A.]"},{"id":"3638771957c3","b":"EPH","v":"npnf.chrysostomus.comm_gal","w":"chrysostomus.comm_gal","a":"johannes_chrysostomus","s":2,"p":[58,58],"r":[6,12],"k":"quotation","m":"editionCitation","c":"high","cited":"[\"Flesh and blood,\" is twice used elsewhere (Mat. 16:17 and Eph. 6:12,) to denote \"weak human nature,\" \"feeble man.\"-G. A.]"},{"id":"440433a51405","b":"ACT","v":"npnf.chrysostomus.comm_gal","w":"chrysostomus.comm_gal","a":"johannes_chrysostomus","s":2,"p":[60,60],"r":[15,2],"k":"quotation","m":"editionCitation","c":"high","cited":"Of those who were sent with St. Paul from Antioch to Jerusalem, Barnabas is the only one named in Acts xv:2, and it would rather seem from Ver. 22, that Silas was then at Jerusalem, and did not accompany St. Paul till his return from thence."},{"id":"5242088e5011","b":"ISA","v":"npnf.chrysostomus.comm_gal","w":"chrysostomus.comm_gal","a":"johannes_chrysostomus","s":2,"p":[60,60],"r":[5,21],"k":"quotation","m":"editionCitation","c":"high","cited":"Isa. v: 21"},{"id":"1fe0f10fc6f4","b":"ROM","v":"npnf.chrysostomus.comm_gal","w":"chrysostomus.comm_gal","a":"johannes_chrysostomus","s":2,"p":[60,60],"r":[12,16],"k":"quotation","m":"editionCitation","c":"high","cited":"Rom. xii: 16"},{"id":"d101f5f86e67","b":"2CO","v":"npnf.chrysostomus.comm_gal","w":"chrysostomus.comm_gal","a":"johannes_chrysostomus","s":2,"p":[64,64],"r":[11,32],"k":"quotation","m":"editionCitation","c":"high","cited":"2 Cor. xi: 32"},{"id":"bd2a14bb0e73","b":"ACT","v":"npnf.chrysostomus.comm_gal","w":"chrysostomus.comm_gal","a":"johannes_chrysostomus","s":2,"p":[65,65],"r":[9,26],"k":"quotation","m":"editionCitation","c":"high","cited":"[First visit to Jerusalem, Acts ix:26. For a reconciliation of the two accounts of this visit see Handy Com. on Gal. Excursus A (by Sanday).-G.A.]"},{"id":"f45638a622bc","b":"ACT","v":"npnf.chrysostomus.comm_gal","w":"chrysostomus.comm_gal","a":"johannes_chrysostomus","s":2,"p":[66,66],"r":[21,17],"k":"quotation","m":"editionCitation","c":"high","cited":"Acts xxi: 17"},{"id":"d61ec9dfda85","b":"ACT","v":"npnf.chrysostomus.comm_gal","w":"chrysostomus.comm_gal","a":"johannes_chrysostomus","s":2,"p":[66,66],"r":[21,20],"k":"quotation","m":"editionCitation","c":"high","cited":"Acts xxi: 20"},{"id":"b343a3fed13c","b":"1CO","v":"npnf.chrysostomus.comm_gal","w":"chrysostomus.comm_gal","a":"johannes_chrysostomus","s":2,"p":[69,69],"r":[15,8],"k":"quotation","m":"editionCitation","c":"high","cited":"\"Thus this James is distinguished from the circle of the twelve (1 Cor. xv. 8.) to which Peter belonged but included in the number of Apostles in the wider sense, which explains the merely supplementary mention of this Apostle.\"-Meyer."},{"id":"b1a4593c10a0","b":"JHN","v":"npnf.chrysostomus.comm_gal","w":"chrysostomus.comm_gal","a":"johannes_chrysostomus","s":2,"p":[70,70],"r":[19,25],"k":"quotation","m":"editionCitation","c":"high","cited":"[Compare John xix:25 with Matt. xxvii:56. But see Lightfoot's learned and exhaustive essay on \"The Brethren of the Lord,\" Com. on Gal. pp. 88-127, and Schaff, Church History, I , 272-275.-G.A.]"},{"id":"a12868c77fd2","b":"MAT","v":"npnf.chrysostomus.comm_gal","w":"chrysostomus.comm_gal","a":"johannes_chrysostomus","s":2,"p":[70,70],"r":[27,56],"k":"quotation","m":"editionCitation","c":"high","cited":"[Compare John xix:25 with Matt. xxvii:56. But see Lightfoot's learned and exhaustive essay on \"The Brethren of the Lord,\" Com. on Gal. pp. 88-127, and Schaff, Church History, I , 272-275.-G.A.]"},{"id":"c843e3eff09f","b":"ACT","v":"npnf.chrysostomus.comm_gal","w":"chrysostomus.comm_gal","a":"johannes_chrysostomus","s":2,"p":[73,73],"r":[9,30],"k":"quotation","m":"editionCitation","c":"high","cited":"[Compare Acts ix:30, where Luke says the brethren took Paul to Caesarea, and thence despatched him to Tarsus (in Cilicia.-G. A.]"},{"id":"f01eb728484c","b":"GAL","v":"npnf.chrysostomus.comm_gal","w":"chrysostomus.comm_gal","a":"johannes_chrysostomus","s":3,"p":[0,0],"r":[1,18],"k":"quotation","m":"editionCitation","c":"high","cited":"[\"The Acts mention five such journeys after his conversion: (1.)-ix:23 (Comp. Gal. i:18.) (2.)-xi:30; xii:25. (3.)-xv:2, the journey to the Apostolic Council, a.d. 50 or 51. (4.)-xviii:22, the Journey in 54. (5.)-xxi:15 (Comp. Ro. 15:25 ff.) the last journey when he was made a pardoner and sent to Caesarea in 58. The first of these journeys cannot be meant on account of Gal. i:18. The second is excluded by the chronological date of Gal. ii:1, for as it took place during the famine of Palestine in the year of Herod's death, a.d. 44, it would put the commission of Paul back to the year 30, which is much too early. There is no good reason why Paul should have mentioned this second journey. The fifth journey cannot be meant for it took place after the composition of Epistle to Galatians and after dispersion of Apostles. Nor can we think of the fourth journey which was transient, nor was Barnabas with him on that journey, Acts xv:39. So the journey here mentioned is the same as that of Acts xv:2. This took place 50 or 51, i. e., fourteen years after his conversion, 37.\"-Schaff in Pop. Com. -G. A.]"},{"id":"91fb04fb9043","b":"GAL","v":"npnf.chrysostomus.comm_gal","w":"chrysostomus.comm_gal","a":"johannes_chrysostomus","s":3,"p":[0,0],"r":[2,1],"k":"verseCommentary","m":"editionCitation","c":"high","cited":"[\"The Acts mention five such journeys after his conversion: (1.)-ix:23 (Comp. Gal. i:18.) (2.)-xi:30; xii:25. (3.)-xv:2, the journey to the Apostolic Council, a.d. 50 or 51. (4.)-xviii:22, the Journey in 54. (5.)-xxi:15 (Comp. Ro. 15:25 ff.) the last journey when he was made a pardoner and sent to Caesarea in 58. The first of these journeys cannot be meant on account of Gal. i:18. The second is excluded by the chronological date of Gal. ii:1, for as it took place during the famine of Palestine in the year of Herod's death, a.d. 44, it would put the commission of Paul back to the year 30, which is much too early. There is no good reason why Paul should have mentioned this second journey. The fifth journey cannot be meant for it took place after the composition of Epistle to Galatians and after dispersion of Apostles. Nor can we think of the fourth journey which was transient, nor was Barnabas with him on that journey, Acts xv:39. So the journey here mentioned is the same as that of Acts xv:2. This took place 50 or 51, i. e., fourteen years after his conversion, 37.\"-Schaff in Pop. Com. -G. A.]"},{"id":"789bf4981db0","b":"ACT","v":"npnf.chrysostomus.comm_gal","w":"chrysostomus.comm_gal","a":"johannes_chrysostomus","s":3,"p":[0,0],"r":[15,39],"k":"quotation","m":"editionCitation","c":"high","cited