is second journey. The fifth journey cannot be meant for it took place after the composition of Epistle to Galatians and after dispersion of Apostles. Nor can we think of the fourth journey which was transient, nor was Barnabas with him on that journey, Acts xv:39. So the journey here mentioned is the same as that of Acts xv:2. This took place 50 or 51, i. e., fourteen years after his conversion, 37.\"-Schaff in Pop. Com. -G. A.]"},{"id":"fd4bbad0ad23","b":"1CO","v":"npnf.chrysostomus.comm_gal","w":"chrysostomus.comm_gal","a":"johannes_chrysostomus","s":3,"p":[3,3],"r":[9,26],"k":"quotation","m":"editionCitation","c":"high","cited":"1 Cor. ix: 26"},{"id":"77ec36de343e","b":"ACT","v":"npnf.chrysostomus.comm_gal","w":"chrysostomus.comm_gal","a":"johannes_chrysostomus","s":3,"p":[4,4],"r":[15,2],"k":"quotation","m":"editionCitation","c":"high","cited":"[\"In St. Luke's narrative (Acts xv:2.) he is said to have been sent by the Church at Antioch. The revelation either prompted or confirmed the decision of the Church.\"-Lightfoot.-G. A.]"},{"id":"1ecba421f1ba","b":"ACT","v":"npnf.chrysostomus.comm_gal","w":"chrysostomus.comm_gal","a":"johannes_chrysostomus","s":3,"p":[4,4],"r":[21,20],"k":"quotation","m":"editionCitation","c":"high","cited":"Acts xxi: 20"},{"id":"e279da83133e","b":"ACT","v":"npnf.chrysostomus.comm_gal","w":"chrysostomus.comm_gal","a":"johannes_chrysostomus","s":3,"p":[8,8],"r":[15,5],"k":"quotation","m":"editionCitation","c":"high","cited":"[\"These were formerly Pharisees (Acts xv:5.) and were still so in spirit although they professed Christianity and were baptized.\" Schaff in Pop. Com. -G. A.]"},{"id":"536b0e9bf380","b":"1CO","v":"npnf.chrysostomus.comm_gal","w":"chrysostomus.comm_gal","a":"johannes_chrysostomus","s":3,"p":[8,8],"r":[7,5],"k":"quotation","m":"editionCitation","c":"high","cited":"1 Cor. vii: 5"},{"id":"5cc1e65469f2","b":"1CO","v":"npnf.chrysostomus.comm_gal","w":"chrysostomus.comm_gal","a":"johannes_chrysostomus","s":3,"p":[8,8],"r":[7,7],"k":"quotation","m":"editionCitation","c":"high","cited":"1 Cor. vii: 7"},{"id":"3777ab78adad","b":"ACT","v":"npnf.chrysostomus.comm_gal","w":"chrysostomus.comm_gal","a":"johannes_chrysostomus","s":3,"p":[11,11],"r":[15,5],"k":"quotation","m":"editionCitation","c":"high","cited":"[\"Had we consented to the suggestion to circumcise Titus, we should thereby have yielded to the false brethren standing in the background, who declared the circumcision of Gentile Christians to be necessary (Acts xv:5.); but this did not at all take place.\"-Meyer.-G. A.]"},{"id":"df94c4d076c0","b":"2CO","v":"npnf.chrysostomus.comm_gal","w":"chrysostomus.comm_gal","a":"johannes_chrysostomus","s":3,"p":[14,14],"r":[5,17],"k":"quotation","m":"editionCitation","c":"high","cited":"2 Cor. v: 17"},{"id":"7363a13c7323","b":"GAL","v":"npnf.chrysostomus.comm_gal","w":"chrysostomus.comm_gal","a":"johannes_chrysostomus","s":3,"p":[14,14],"r":[5,2],"k":"quotation","m":"editionCitation","c":"high","cited":"Gal. v: 2"},{"id":"7ac1f6fc5e1a","b":"1CO","v":"npnf.chrysostomus.comm_gal","w":"chrysostomus.comm_gal","a":"johannes_chrysostomus","s":3,"p":[27,27],"r":[9,20],"k":"quotation","m":"editionCitation","c":"high","cited":"[\"There was no difference of doctrine or gospel, but only a division of territory, and how little Paul considered his apostolic call to the `Gentiles 0' as excluding the conversion of the Jews from his operations may be seen from such passages as 1 Cor. ix:20; Ro. i:16; ix:1; xi:14.\"-Meyer.-G. A.]"},{"id":"c8b7a7f78096","b":"HEB","v":"npnf.chrysostomus.comm_gal","w":"chrysostomus.comm_gal","a":"johannes_chrysostomus","s":3,"p":[30,30],"r":[10,34],"k":"quotation","m":"editionCitation","c":"high","cited":"[Hebrews x:34 [This is interesting as showing that Chrysostom attributed the Epistle to the Hebrews to St. Paul, though most modern critics do not agree with him in that view.-G. A.]"},{"id":"7b63a8c00173","b":"1CO","v":"npnf.chrysostomus.comm_gal","w":"chrysostomus.comm_gal","a":"johannes_chrysostomus","s":3,"p":[30,30],"r":[16,1,16,3],"k":"quotation","m":"editionCitation","c":"high","cited":"1 Cor. xvi: 1-3"},{"id":"47fb6b7e8e28","b":"MAT","v":"npnf.chrysostomus.comm_gal","w":"chrysostomus.comm_gal","a":"johannes_chrysostomus","s":3,"p":[33,33],"r":[16,16],"k":"quotation","m":"editionCitation","c":"high","cited":"Mat. xvi: 16"},{"id":"17f86a447369","b":"MAT","v":"npnf.chrysostomus.comm_gal","w":"chrysostomus.comm_gal","a":"johannes_chrysostomus","s":3,"p":[33,33],"r":[17,4],"k":"quotation","m":"editionCitation","c":"high","cited":"Mat. xvii: 4"},{"id":"b8445077bfac","b":"MAT","v":"npnf.chrysostomus.comm_gal","w":"chrysostomus.comm_gal","a":"johannes_chrysostomus","s":3,"p":[33,33],"r":[16,22],"k":"quotation","m":"editionCitation","c":"high","cited":"Mat. xvi: 22"},{"id":"e7c8a2edf89c","b":"JHN","v":"npnf.chrysostomus.comm_gal","w":"chrysostomus.comm_gal","a":"johannes_chrysostomus","s":3,"p":[33,33],"r":[21,7],"k":"quotation","m":"editionCitation","c":"high","cited":"John xxi: 7"},{"id":"f9415cd0b7ff","b":"ACT","v":"npnf.chrysostomus.comm_gal","w":"chrysostomus.comm_gal","a":"johannes_chrysostomus","s":3,"p":[33,33],"r":[2,14],"k":"quotation","m":"editionCitation","c":"high","cited":"Acts ii: 14"},{"id":"cdc24440de85","b":"ACT","v":"npnf.chrysostomus.comm_gal","w":"chrysostomus.comm_gal","a":"johannes_chrysostomus","s":3,"p":[33,33],"r":[2,36],"k":"quotation","m":"editionCitation","c":"high","cited":"Acts 2:36"},{"id":"4f649538d2bd","b":"2CO","v":"npnf.chrysostomus.comm_gal","w":"chrysostomus.comm_gal","a":"johannes_chrysostomus","s":3,"p":[35,35],"r":[11,3],"k":"quotation","m":"editionCitation","c":"high","cited":"2 Cor. xi: 3"},{"id":"448e3bdf7639","b":"ROM","v":"npnf.chrysostomus.comm_gal","w":"chrysostomus.comm_gal","a":"johannes_chrysostomus","s":3,"p":[45,45],"r":[15,25],"k":"quotation","m":"editionCitation","c":"high","cited":"Rom. xv: 25"},{"id":"61fcc2d37ac2","b":"ROM","v":"npnf.chrysostomus.comm_gal","w":"chrysostomus.comm_gal","a":"johannes_chrysostomus","s":3,"p":[45,45],"r":[15,26],"k":"quotation","m":"editionCitation","c":"high","cited":"Rom. xv: 26"},{"id":"d5b2a8765ecb","b":"DEU","v":"npnf.chrysostomus.comm_gal","w":"chrysostomus.comm_gal","a":"johannes_chrysostomus","s":3,"p":[54,54],"r":[18,15],"k":"quotation","m":"editionCitation","c":"high","cited":"[\"This second interpretation of Chrysostom is undoubtedly the correct one (though he errs in elucidating the relation of δια; by referring to Deut. xviii:15.) comp. Rom. vii:4, 6; The law itself led him to Christ, by developing the sense of sin and the need of redemption.\"-Schaff in Pop. Com .-G. A.]"},{"id":"bfdb63f4932f","b":"ROM","v":"npnf.chrysostomus.comm_gal","w":"chrysostomus.comm_gal","a":"johannes_chrysostomus","s":3,"p":[54,54],"r":[7,4],"k":"quotation","m":"editionCitation","c":"high","cited":"[\"This second interpretation of Chrysostom is undoubtedly the correct one (though he errs in elucidating the relation of δια; by referring to Deut. xviii:15.) comp. Rom. vii:4, 6; The law itself led him to Christ, by developing the sense of sin and the need of redemption.\"-Schaff in Pop. Com .-G. A.]"},{"id":"84b7d3401b2b","b":"ROM","v":"npnf.chrysostomus.comm_gal","w":"chrysostomus.comm_gal","a":"johannes_chrysostomus","s":3,"p":[55,55],"r":[8,2],"k":"quotation","m":"editionCitation","c":"high","cited":"Rom. viii: 2"},{"id":"73816c952a9c","b":"DEU","v":"npnf.chrysostomus.comm_gal","w":"chrysostomus.comm_gal","a":"johannes_chrysostomus","s":3,"p":[55,55],"r":[18,15],"k":"quotation","m":"editionCitation","c":"high","cited":"Deut. xviii: 15"},{"id":"2c0cae7987fb","b":"COL","v":"npnf.chrysostomus.comm_gal","w":"chrysostomus.comm_gal","a":"johannes_chrysostomus","s":3,"p":[58,58],"r":[3,5],"k":"quotation","m":"editionCitation","c":"high","cited":"Col. iii: 5"},{"id":"6d3f2c6adec7","b":"ROM","v":"npnf.chrysostomus.comm_gal","w":"chrysostomus.comm_gal","a":"johannes_chrysostomus","s":3,"p":[58,58],"r":[6,6],"k":"quotation","m":"editionCitation","c":"high","cited":"Rom. vi: 6"},{"id":"f18029274617","b":"ROM","v":"npnf.chrysostomus.comm_gal","w":"chrysostomus.comm_gal","a":"johannes_chrysostomus","s":3,"p":[60,60],"r":[3,23],"k":"quotation","m":"editionCitation","c":"high","cited":"Rom. iii: 23"},{"id":"08c001c294ac","b":"JHN","v":"npnf.chrysostomus.comm_gal","w":"chrysostomus.comm_gal","a":"johannes_chrysostomus","s":3,"p":[62,62],"r":[3,16],"k":"quotation","m":"editionCitation","c":"high","cited":"John iii: 16"},{"id":"a48e75614803","b":"ROM","v":"npnf.chrysostomus.comm_gal","w":"chrysostomus.comm_gal","a":"johannes_chrysostomus","s":3,"p":[62,62],"r":[8,32],"k":"quotation","m":"editionCitation","c":"high","cited":"Rom. viii: 32"},{"id":"412e0b455c37","b":"TIT","v":"npnf.chrysostomus.comm_gal","w":"chrysostomus.comm_gal","a":"johannes_chrysostomus","s":3,"p":[62,62],"r":[2,14],"k":"quotation","m":"editionCitation","c":"high","cited":"Tit. ii: 14"},{"id":"4115701cf21c","b":"LUK","v":"npnf.chrysostomus.comm_gal","w":"chrysostomus.comm_gal","a":"johannes_chrysostomus","s":3,"p":[62,62],"r":[14,16],"k":"quotation","m":"editionCitation","c":"high","cited":"Luke xiv: 16"},{"id":"50c5de15650a","b":"MAT","v":"npnf.chrysostomus.comm_gal","w":"chrysostomus.comm_gal","a":"johannes_chrysostomus","s":3,"p":[62,62],"r":[18,12],"k":"quotation","m":"editionCitation","c":"high","cited":"Mat. xviii: 12"},{"id":"15472bbcdd7b","b":"ROM","v":"npnf.chrysostomus.comm_gal","w":"chrysostomus.comm_gal","a":"johannes_chrysostomus","s":3,"p":[62,62],"r":[3,3],"k":"quotation","m":"editionCitation","c":"high","cited":"Rom. iii: 3"},{"id":"914abada269e","b":"GAL","v":"npnf.chrysostomus.comm_gal","w":"chrysostomus.comm_gal","a":"johannes_chrysostomus","s":4,"p":[1,1],"r":[1,6],"k":"quotation","m":"editionCitation","c":"high","cited":"Gal. i: 6"},{"id":"5727728e07a3","b":"MAT","v":"npnf.chrysostomus.comm_gal","w":"chrysostomus.comm_gal","a":"johannes_chrysostomus","s":4,"p":[1,1],"r":[5,22],"k":"quotation","m":"editionCitation","c":"high","cited":"Mat. v: 22"},{"id":"dde841e2c36b","b":"GAL","v":"npnf.chrysostomus.comm_gal","w":"chrysostomus.comm_gal","a":"johannes_chrysostomus","s":4,"p":[4,4],"r":[5,11],"k":"quotation","m":"editionCitation","c":"high","cited":"[\"As we know nothing of persecutions endured by Galatians, it seems preferable to take the word in a neutral sense embracing all spiritual experiences (blessings and benefits as well) of the Galatians.(Comp. v.3 and 6.)\"-Schaff. Lightfoot refers it to the persecutions endured by the Galatians from Jews citing Gal. v:11; and says \"the ἐί γε leaves a loophole for doubt which the καί, following, widens.\" So Ellicott. Meyer says, \"It refers to everything which the false apostles in their Judaistic zeal had troubled and burdened the Galatians with. The εἰκῆ then means \"and all to no profit, all in vain,\" if indeed it be only (καί) in vain and not to the positive risk of your Messianic salvation that ye have suffered.\"-G. A.]"},{"id":"bbcd343ae240","b":"GAL","v":"npnf.chrysostomus.comm_gal","w":"chrysostomus.comm_gal","a":"johannes_chrysostomus","s":4,"p":[12,12],"r":[5,4],"k":"quotation","m":"editionCitation","c":"high","cited":"Gal. v: 4"},{"id":"4d5b874421d8","b":"DEU","v":"npnf.chrysostomus.comm_gal","w":"chrysostomus.comm_gal","a":"johannes_chrysostomus","s":4,"p":[18,18],"r":[21,23],"k":"quotation","m":"editionCitation","c":"high","cited":"[\"A parenthetic justification from Deut. xxi:23 of the startling expression just used. The passage refers to those criminals who, alter being stoned, were hung upon a stake, but were not permitted to remain over night lest the holy land should be desecrated. Our Saviour fulfilled the legal curse by hanging dead on the cross. This is one of the strongest passages for the doctrine of a vicarious atonement. The vicarious efficacy lies not so much in the preposition, ὑπέρ,’ `for, 0' as in the whole sentence.\"-Schaff-G. A.]"},{"id":"129c92f768c3","b":"DEU","v":"npnf.chrysostomus.comm_gal","w":"chrysostomus.comm_gal","a":"johannes_chrysostomus","s":4,"p":[21,21],"r":[27,26],"k":"quotation","m":"editionCitation","c":"high","cited":"Deut. xxvii: 26"},{"id":"77c205919118","b":"GEN","v":"npnf.chrysostomus.comm_gal","w":"chrysostomus.comm_gal","a":"johannes_chrysostomus","s":4,"p":[21,21],"r":[12,4],"k":"quotation","m":"editionCitation","c":"high","cited":"Gen. xii: 4"},{"id":"e7f0019d3ca6","b":"HAB","v":"npnf.chrysostomus.comm_gal","w":"chrysostomus.comm_gal","a":"johannes_chrysostomus","s":4,"p":[27,27],"r":[2,4],"k":"quotation","m":"editionCitation","c":"high","cited":"Hab. ii: 4"},{"id":"fcf3c1621106","b":"EPH","v":"npnf.chrysostomus.comm_gal","w":"chrysostomus.comm_gal","a":"johannes_chrysostomus","s":4,"p":[29,29],"r":[2,8],"k":"quotation","m":"editionCitation","c":"high","cited":"Eph. ii: 8"},{"id":"f529e8a089e1","b":"ROM","v":"npnf.chrysostomus.comm_gal","w":"chrysostomus.comm_gal","a":"johannes_chrysostomus","s":4,"p":[30,30],"r":[8,3],"k":"quotation","m":"editionCitation","c":"high","cited":"Rom. viii: 3"},{"id":"59ffcd68443f","b":"DEU","v":"npnf.chrysostomus.comm_gal","w":"chrysostomus.comm_gal","a":"johannes_chrysostomus","s":4,"p":[32,32],"r":[27,26],"k":"quotation","m":"editionCitation","c":"high","cited":"Deut. xxvii: 26"},{"id":"e4a1db4668d6","b":"ISA","v":"npnf.chrysostomus.comm_gal","w":"chrysostomus.comm_gal","a":"johannes_chrysostomus","s":4,"p":[32,32],"r":[53,9],"k":"quotation","m":"editionCitation","c":"high","cited":"Isa. liii: 9"},{"id":"c1e3d6903d36","b":"1PE","v":"npnf.chrysostomus.comm_gal","w":"chrysostomus.comm_gal","a":"johannes_chrysostomus","s":4,"p":[32,32],"r":[2,22],"k":"quotation","m":"editionCitation","c":"high","cited":"1 Peter ii: 22"},{"id":"af9c0828b20f","b":"EPH","v":"npnf.chrysostomus.comm_gal","w":"chrysostomus.comm_gal","a":"johannes_chrysostomus","s":4,"p":[34,34],"r":[1,23],"k":"quotation","m":"editionCitation","c":"high","cited":"[\"Not as a single individual but as Head of the church which is His body, Eph. 1:23. The key to the passage is in ver. 28 and 29: `Ye are all one in Christ Jesus. 0' \"-Schaff.-G. A.]"},{"id":"9fe7cdef4356","b":"GEN","v":"npnf.chrysostomus.comm_gal","w":"chrysostomus.comm_gal","a":"johannes_chrysostomus","s":4,"p":[34,34],"r":[22,18],"k":"quotation","m":"editionCitation","c":"high","cited":"Gen. xxii: 18"},{"id":"28f1ddd03704","b":"1CO","v":"npnf.chrysostomus.comm_gal","w":"chrysostomus.comm_gal","a":"johannes_chrysostomus","s":4,"p":[36,36],"r":[9,7],"k":"quotation","m":"editionCitation","c":"high","cited":"1 Cor. ix: 7"},{"id":"5eff9256cee7","b":"HEB","v":"npnf.chrysostomus.comm_gal","w":"chrysostomus.comm_gal","a":"johannes_chrysostomus","s":4,"p":[36,36],"r":[9,17],"k":"quotation","m":"editionCitation","c":"high","cited":"Heb. ix: 17"},{"id":"6a211ead5dea","b":"ISA","v":"npnf.chrysostomus.comm_gal","w":"chrysostomus.comm_gal","a":"johannes_chrysostomus","s":4,"p":[36,36],"r":[49,15],"k":"quotation","m":"editionCitation","c":"high","cited":"Isa. xlix: 15"},{"id":"c2805537d25b","b":"ISA","v":"npnf.chrysostomus.comm_gal","w":"chrysostomus.comm_gal","a":"johannes_chrysostomus","s":4,"p":[36,36],"r":[45,9],"k":"quotation","m":"editionCitation","c":"high","cited":"Isa. xlv: 9"},{"id":"79a92c2a4a97","b":"HOS","v":"npnf.chrysostomus.comm_gal","w":"chrysostomus.comm_gal","a":"johannes_chrysostomus","s":4,"p":[36,36],"r":[2,7],"k":"quotation","m":"editionCitation","c":"medium","cited":"Hos. ii: 5","note":"Stellenangabe der Ausgabe (englische Zählung, umgerechnet)"},{"id":"e52b4d66afa4","b":"JER","v":"npnf.chrysostomus.comm_gal","w":"chrysostomus.comm_gal","a":"johannes_chrysostomus","s":4,"p":[36,36],"r":[18,1,18,6],"k":"quotation","m":"editionCitation","c":"high","cited":"Jer. xviii: 1-6"},{"id":"ebae18d2c39e","b":"DEU","v":"npnf.chrysostomus.comm_gal","w":"chrysostomus.comm_gal","a":"johannes_chrysostomus","s":4,"p":[37,37],"r":[5,5],"k":"quotation","m":"editionCitation","c":"high","cited":"[\"We may reasonably wonder,\" says Ellicott, \"how the early expositors (Basil and Theodoret excepted) could have so generally coincided in the perplexing view of Origen that the Mediator here mentioned was Christ. On the contrary it is plain that it was Moses, Deut. v:5.\"-G. A.]"},{"id":"ffea8f33aead","b":"ROM","v":"npnf.chrysostomus.comm_gal","w":"chrysostomus.comm_gal","a":"johannes_chrysostomus","s":4,"p":[53,53],"r":[10,3],"k":"quotation","m":"editionCitation","c":"high","cited":"Rom. x: 3"},{"id":"25ff9856bf8c","b":"1CO","v":"npnf.chrysostomus.comm_gal","w":"chrysostomus.comm_gal","a":"johannes_chrysostomus","s":5,"p":[13,13],"r":[12,31],"k":"quotation","m":"editionCitation","c":"high","cited":"[This word does not here mean \"they vie with you,\" as Chrysostom interprets it, but \"they zealously seek you or pay court to you,\" (1 Cor. xii:31).-G. A.]"},{"id":"87c36ff8ac39","b":"1CO","v":"npnf.chrysostomus.comm_gal","w":"chrysostomus.comm_gal","a":"johannes_chrysostomus","s":5,"p":[27,27],"r":[10,11],"k":"quotation","m":"editionCitation","c":"high","cited":"[\"The story of Hagar and Sarah has another (namely a figurative, typical) meaning besides (not instead of) the literal or historical. Paul does not deny the fact but makes it the bearer of a general idea which was more fully expressed in two covenants. He uses allegorical here in a sense similar to the word \"typical\" in 1 Cor. x:11.\"-Schaff.-G. A.] [See on this difficult passage Schaff's Excursus in Com. and Lightfoot's Excursus xiii. Com. p. 368.-G. A.]"},{"id":"2ad4de41a969","b":"ACT","v":"npnf.chrysostomus.comm_gal","w":"chrysostomus.comm_gal","a":"johannes_chrysostomus","s":5,"p":[30,30],"r":[20,31],"k":"quotation","m":"editionCitation","c":"high","cited":"Acts xx: 31"},{"id":"01b327da6177","b":"GEN","v":"npnf.chrysostomus.comm_gal","w":"chrysostomus.comm_gal","a":"johannes_chrysostomus","s":5,"p":[33,33],"r":[15,16],"k":"quotation","m":"editionCitation","c":"high","cited":"Gen. xv: 16"},{"id":"680d9a4cb3fe","b":"GEN","v":"npnf.chrysostomus.comm_gal","w":"chrysostomus.comm_gal","a":"johannes_chrysostomus","s":5,"p":[52,52],"r":[18,14],"k":"quotation","m":"editionCitation","c":"high","cited":"Gen. xviii: 14"},{"id":"e017514390ab","b":"GEN","v":"npnf.chrysostomus.comm_gal","w":"chrysostomus.comm_gal","a":"johannes_chrysostomus","s":5,"p":[54,54],"r":[21,10],"k":"quotation","m":"editionCitation","c":"high","cited":"Gen. xxi: 10"},{"id":"16cac3ab437f","b":"PHP","v":"npnf.chrysostomus.comm_gal","w":"chrysostomus.comm_gal","a":"johannes_chrysostomus","s":6,"p":[16,16],"r":[3,2],"k":"quotation","m":"editionCitation","c":"high","cited":"[\"The vivid realization of the doings of his opponents, who were not ashamed to resort even to such falsehood, now wrings from his soul a strong and bitterly sarcastic wish of holy indignation.\"-Meyer. Paul wishes that the circumcisers would not stop with circumcision but go beyond it to mutilation (make themselves eunuchs) like the priests of Cybele. A severe irony and similar to the one in Phil. iii:2, 3, where Paul calls the boasters of circumcision \"the Concision.\" Self mutilation was a recognized form of heathen worship especially in Pessinus in Galatia and therefore quite familiar to the readers. Thus by their glorying in the flesh the Galatians relapsed into their former heathenism,-Schaff and Lightfoot. The Revised Version here has, \"would even cut themselves off,\" the American Committee has, \"would go beyond circumcision.\"-G. A.]"},{"id":"b197a46404f8","b":"GAL","v":"npnf.chrysostomus.comm_gal","w":"chrysostomus.comm_gal","a":"johannes_chrysostomus","s":6,"p":[18,18],"r":[3,1],"k":"quotation","m":"editionCitation","c":"high","cited":"Gal. iii: 1"},{"id":"3b0c88d9a5ce","b":"ACT","v":"npnf.chrysostomus.comm_gal","w":"chrysostomus.comm_gal","a":"johannes_chrysostomus","s":6,"p":[29,29],"r":[6,13],"k":"quotation","m":"editionCitation","c":"high","cited":"Acts vi: 13"},{"id":"83039173bd30","b":"ACT","v":"npnf.chrysostomus.comm_gal","w":"chrysostomus.comm_gal","a":"johannes_chrysostomus","s":6,"p":[29,29],"r":[21,29],"k":"quotation","m":"editionCitation","c":"high","cited":"Acts xxi: 29"},{"id":"cb29877ff947","b":"TIT","v":"npnf.chrysostomus.comm_gal","w":"chrysostomus.comm_gal","a":"johannes_chrysostomus","s":6,"p":[31,31],"r":[3,10],"k":"quotation","m":"editionCitation","c":"high","cited":"Tit. iii: 10"},{"id":"10be5abac8ec","b":"1SA","v":"npnf.chrysostomus.comm_gal","w":"chrysostomus.comm_gal","a":"johannes_chrysostomus","s":6,"p":[43,43],"r":[20,4],"k":"quotation","m":"editionCitation","c":"high","cited":"1 Sam. xx: 4"},{"id":"b636a036e8d1","b":"PSA","v":"npnf.chrysostomus.comm_gal","w":"chrysostomus.comm_gal","a":"johannes_chrysostomus","s":6,"p":[43,43],"r":[42,2],"k":"quotation","m":"editionCitation","c":"medium","cited":"Ps. xlii: 1","note":"Stellenangabe der Ausgabe (englische Zählung, umgerechnet)"},{"id":"b5ff1bae9b5b","b":"ROM","v":"npnf.chrysostomus.comm_gal","w":"chrysostomus.comm_gal","a":"johannes_chrysostomus","s":6,"p":[43,43],"r":[8,8],"k":"quotation","m":"editionCitation","c":"high","cited":"Rom. viii: 8"},{"id":"a18426d561d6","b":"ROM","v":"npnf.chrysostomus.comm_gal","w":"chrysostomus.comm_gal","a":"johannes_chrysostomus","s":6,"p":[43,43],"r":[8,9],"k":"quotation","m":"editionCitation","c":"high","cited":"Rom. viii: 9"},{"id":"e8cedecab579","b":"JHN","v":"npnf.chrysostomus.comm_gal","w":"chrysostomus.comm_gal","a":"johannes_chrysostomus","s":6,"p":[43,43],"r":[8,44],"k":"quotation","m":"editionCitation","c":"high","cited":"John viii: 44"},{"id":"19ef74c20c19","b":"1CO","v":"npnf.chrysostomus.comm_gal","w":"chrysostomus.comm_gal","a":"johannes_chrysostomus","s":6,"p":[43,43],"r":[11,14],"k":"quotation","m":"editionCitation","c":"high","cited":"1 Cor. 11: 14"},{"id":"717ab18f89e3","b":"EPH","v":"npnf.chrysostomus.comm_gal","w":"chrysostomus.comm_gal","a":"johannes_chrysostomus","s":6,"p":[43,43],"r":[6,12],"k":"quotation","m":"editionCitation","c":"high","cited":"Eph. vi: 12"},{"id":"f47541767b58","b":"COL","v":"npnf.chrys